<title>ITALY: Pirelli denies rumour of Bridgestone buy.</title>
<headline>Pirelli denies rumour of Bridgestone buy.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian tyre and cable maker Pirelli SpA on Tuesday denied a Tokyo market rumour about a possible sale of its Pirelli-Armstrong U.S. tyre unit to Bridgestone Corp Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Pirelli-Armstrong USA in not on sale. Pirelli is fully committed to the U.S. market both as a manufacturer and supplier,&quot; a Pirelli spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Earlier in Tokyo, Bridgestone denied the rumour. &quot;I have not heard that we are buying the company,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Bridgestone shares jumped to a record high of 2,150 yen soon after the Tokyo stock market opening.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 6129589</p>
</text>
